## Dev workflow

| Command | Purpose |
| ------- | ------- |
| `yarn tauri:dev` | Full desktop app |
| `yarn dev` | Frontend only + mock API (faster UI iteration) |
| `yarn test:e2e:ui` | Debug Playwright interactively |

Browser dev sets theme via `localStorage.setItem('orbit.themeId', 'orbit')` in E2E boot helper.


Library and Search share Installed / All games on `LibraryEntry` identity; Favorites
is added only when at least one title is marked favorite. Search still hides view tabs.
Installed is disk copies (including additional Windows Steam library folders). All games
includes owned titles that are not installed. Home uses the same entries. Details is one
page for installed, owned-not-installed, and unavailable titles. Windows Steam Play goes
through `play_steam_windows_game`. Home and Details enable Play when `signedIn`
and the Windows install is available. Downloads write into
`runtimes/containers/games/steam-{appId}/install/`. Rust clones a per-game
container from `steam-windows`, seeds login files, and starts the EXE with
`SteamAppId`. Sign-in stops `steam.exe` after saving the login. See
[STEAM_WINDOWS.md](STEAM_WINDOWS.md) and [CONTAINERS.md](CONTAINERS.md).

Home copy, header logo, and shell backdrop share `useHomeHero`, which prepends the selected `LibraryEntry` fetch so a title missing from the first library page still paints its own hero. `useBackdropTransition` keeps at most two backdrop layers in the shell. The browser decodes the incoming image before showing it, ignores late results after selection changes, and caches up to 24 lighting samples. Local artwork can use the Rust lighting command. The webview compositor runs the fades.


Glass surfaces share the material loaded by `GlassMaterialBootstrap`. They use
compositor blur with a Rust-generated texture and do not allocate canvas maps or
subscribe to panel geometry. Browser preview uses the same CSS without the native
grain texture. Translucent cards, buttons, badges, and fields use the same shared material through `orbit-panel` and `orbit-glass-control`.

Keyboard routing lives in `controllers/keyboard.ts`. Backspace has no navigation binding. Global navigation shortcuts yield to input, textarea, select, editable-content, textbox and combobox contexts, consumed events, composition, and system modifier combinations. Escape remains Back outside editing contexts. Dialogs handle Escape locally and preserve IME composition.


Theme cards use `ThemeCardArtwork` with a fixed 2:1 header. Backgrounds cover the
frame; logos remain contained within an inset box. Native sessions use one
streaming thumbnail batch, cached across navigation by TanStack Query. Browser
preview uses the packaged thumbnails generated with the same renderer.
`ArtworkImage` requests asynchronous decoding, keeps a shimmer until decoding
completes, fades the image in, handles errors, and ignores stale decode callbacks.
Reduced Motion disables shimmer and fade. No image decode or resize loop runs in
React rendering.

`useNavigationInput` mirrors input modality onto the document root in O(1) without
rerendering every card. Shared inset outlines cover spatial focus across routes
and body portals. Cover tiles (`orbit-art-focus`) move that ring onto the artwork
so titles sit outside it. Pointer movement, rather than layout-induced mouse enter,
switches back to pointer navigation.

Theme settings reuse the hydrated catalog and packaged previews. Native custom
entries provide runtime-only thumbnail paths; grids never need embedded image
blobs. Preview caches are separate from portable theme JSON. Concurrent catalog
requests share one promise, including StrictMode bootstrap effects. Theme grouping
uses a single O(n) map pass instead of copying the growing groups on each item.

## Runtime controls

Settings → Compatibility uses `modules/settings/components/RuntimeSettings.tsx`.
Settings → Steam uses `modules/settings/components/SteamSettings.tsx` for authorization, offline mode, and file verification. Installing Steam for Windows uses the shared `steam:setup` download task so the progress bar and errors stay visible if the panel unmounts. The Install button stays until `steamwebhelper.exe` is on disk under `cef.win64`, `cef.win7x64`, or `cef.win7`, not merely `steam.exe`.

Details → Settings → Refresh metadata calls `enrich_game_metadata`, which fetches Steam store copy for the known AppID first, then TheGamesDB. Importer stubs such as leftover shortcut install notes are replaced or cleared; catalog overlay never fills an empty field with those stubs.
The primary flow is one managed install action with download/install progress,
online component/version catalog with prereleases and mirror checksums, and
`CompatibilityGlobalSettings.tsx` for defaults.
`CompatibilityOverridesEditor.tsx` stores only explicit per-game overrides in the
shared Wine profile editor. Wine paths and manual registration stay under Advanced
runtime options. The
`CompatibilityStatus.supported` system flag gates managed setup independently
of browser or user-agent checks. `components/runtime/WineProfileEditor.tsx` is
shared by manual `.exe` import and Edit properties. `types/runtime.ts` mirrors
Rust's profile, detected runtime, status and setup progress. Game details retains
Play/Stop and adds cancellation during Windows preparation and bounded diagnostics
through `RuntimeDiagnostics.tsx`. Browser preview cannot download or execute Wine.

### Settings usability and download feedback

Settings presentation uses Tailwind on the settings and Steam components, keeping semantic hooks (`settings-layout`, `settings-tabs`, `settings-content`, `settings-content-scroll`, `settings-insights`, `settings-tab`, `image-search-drawer`, `steam-activity-*`) for E2E. `components/ui/animated-settings-nav.tsx` adapts Aceternity Tabs with Orbit Focusable controls, and `components/ui/switch.tsx` adapts shadcn Switch. `stores/graphics-draft.store.ts` retains an in-memory form draft across navigation; Save calls the existing typed Rust wrapper once, while Discard restores the query result. `modules/settings/hooks/useCompatibilitySetup.ts` retains progress across page unmounts and guards duplicate installations. Complexity: fixed-size graphics comparisons are O(1); catalog rendering is O(total versions), with no per-row I/O or library scans added. No new native command or download trust boundary is introduced.

## Interface editors and loading

`GameSettingsPanel` saves only launch configuration through `updateGame` and owns
an explicit draft initialized per game. `GamePropertiesEditor` owns metadata and
artwork drafts, keyed by game identity; refetches do not reinitialize these fields.
`LibrarySkeleton` renders a fixed eight placeholders without registering controller
focus targets. Runtime option lists use the existing Orbit-styled Radix Select.

Settings owns `useSettingsControllerFocus`, which registers native form controls
not already registered by shared components. Its observer and focus subscription
are cleaned up when the page unmounts. Steam folder preference saves invalidate the
owned-library query so installation badges refresh.

`SteamLibraryFolders` runs Windows import discovery after a successful path save.
Scan results/errors are displayed separately from preference-save errors, and a
Scan installed games action retries discovery for already-saved folders.

`useLaunchProgress` restores the launch failure banner on `game-session-ended` with a nonzero exit code and `process-exited` reason, even after `game-session-started` cleared it. It preserves an existing detailed failure, ignores exits from another game while a launch banner is active, and cleans up listeners that resolve after unmount.

SteamQrModal keeps its host mounted while opening, uses useSteamLoginPlacement for bounded native placement, traps Orbit controller focus, and waits for native cancellation before closing. The browser is ready only when placement succeeds. The host is a native-window placeholder, not embedded Steam HTML.
